From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:45:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 156/342] libdevice: BDigitalPin, BPWM and BGeekPort, the rest
 of the header

Be-style classes for the ODROID-C2's 40-pin header beyond the BeBox
ones, through meson_gpio:

- BDigitalPin: one GPIO pin, "Pin7" or "GPIOX_21": direction, pull,
  level, and edges, waited for (WaitForEdge(), with the level and the
  time) or sent to a BMessenger (B_DIGITAL_PIN_CHANGED).
- BPWM: "PWM1" (pin 11) and "PWM2" (pin 19) with a period and pulse
  width in nanoseconds, or a frequency and duty cycle; 0.33 us steps at
  50 Hz, for servos. Closing stops it, the pin low.
- BGeekPort: all 40 pins, what each can do, what it does now, and who
  has it.

One owner per pin, whatever class asks. 3.3 V pins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
